      "sourceTextSha256": "6f8026eb80d55e3a78e2bbc26a85160f1ed4297251ba96ed668946c7b6ca260d",
      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast at the hotel. Transfer to the airport and flight to Iguazu, where a driver meets you with a sign bearing your names for the transfer to the hotel.\n\nOn the Iguazu River, at the border between Brazil and Argentina, 275 cascades plunge into the gorge known as the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. Walkways and paths bring you remarkably close to the falls, even to the edge of the Devil’s Throat amid clouds of spray, and their roar can be heard for kilometres. Viewing platforms reveal them from both the Brazilian and the Argentine sides.",
